WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.300
HBO is doing everything in its power to keep
the secrets of Game of Thrones’ final season

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.480
under wraps but that hasn't stopped the rumor
mill from whirring away nonetheless.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.420
These are a few of the spoilers that have
slipped out so far.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:18.520
Thanks to a first-look set report from Entertainment
Weekly, we now know exactly how Game of Thrones'

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:19.620
first new episode will begin.

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:24.260
The season will kick off in Winterfell as
Daenerys Targaryen drives her forces to the

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:28.600
North to help Jon Snow and his allies prepare
for battle against the Night King's army.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:33.760
The setup is expected to resemble the pilot
episode's big arrival of Robert Baratheon

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.740
and will usher in some interesting reunions
between various characters.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.620
At least one person will be less than delighted
at the new arrival, though — with Sansa

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:47.020
Stark reportedly being displeased with Jon's
decision to "bend the knee" in allegiance

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:47.900
to Daenerys.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:51.960
Considering what they're all up against, however,
she might just have to get over it.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.020
Executive producer Bryan Cogman told the magazine:

00:00:55.520 --> 00:01:00.200
"It's about all of these disparate characters
coming together to face a common enemy, dealing

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:04.420
with their own past, and defining the person
they want to be in the face of certain death.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:10.120
It's an incredibly emotional, haunting, bittersweet
final season, and I think it honors very much

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.580
what George [R.R. Martin] set out to do."

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:17.670
In addition to Daenerys' journey to Winterfell,
Jaime Lannister is also expected to be heading

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:22.460
in that direction — although Nikolaj Coster-Waldau
couldn't guarantee he'll make it all the way.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:28.000
Viewers of the 76th Golden Globe Awards were
treated to a brief but powerful new teaser

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.260
for Game of Thrones' upcoming season.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:34.320
Although it was a blink-and-you'll-miss-it
reel, the brief clip contained a pretty big

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.420
clue as to what lies ahead for the show.

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:41.200
In the eight-second piece of footage, which
launched alongside a bevy of other HBO teaser

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:46.100
samples, Sansa is shown coming face to face
with the Mother of Dragons at long last.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:50.480
“Winterfell is yours, Your Grace.”

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:54.600
It's hard to tell whether Sansa's gesture
is authentic or if she's become as cunning

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:59.310
as her late ear-whisperer Littlefinger, but
in either case it's clear the Lady of Winterfell

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:04.299
is going to cede some power to Daenerys Targaryen
for one reason or another — which is a pretty

00:02:04.299 --> 00:02:09.090
surprising development given how reluctant
she was to let Jon flit off to Dragonstone

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:10.900
and buddy up with Daenerys in the first place.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:16.820
In January, HBO released a new teaser for
Game of Thrones Season 8 that features Jon

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:21.380
Snow, Sansa Stark, and Arya Stark all convening
in the Stark family crypt.

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:31.320
New to the scene is a trio of statues that
represent the Stark siblings themselves — and,

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.100
notably, Bran Stark is missing.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:38.120
His handicap has certainly never stopped him
from going places before, so it can't realistically

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:40.480
be an access issue which is keeping him at
bay.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:45.459
Instead, his absence from the teaser may be
a bit of an official wink to the long-held

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:50.040
fan theory that Bran Stark will become the
Night King during one of his wargs back in

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:50.540
time.

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:54.960
The idea is that, since Bran has been able
to affect certain aspects of history in the

00:02:54.980 --> 00:03:00.400
past, he may inadvertently be the one to cause
the ice zombie's ascent in the first place.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:05.760
Although she's currently persona non grata
with Jon Snow and the rest of the north, Melisandre

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:08.940
isn't done with her work for the Lord of Light
just yet.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:14.420
“Oh, I will return Despila one last time.”

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:15.480
“My lady.”

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:19.860
“I have to die in the strange country...
just like you.”

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:24.730
Some fans theorize that the reason the Red
Woman is headed off to the free city of Volantis

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:25.900
is to earn redemption.

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:30.650
If she is able to recruit the Fiery Hand,
the 1,000 soldiers who guard the city and

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:35.150
follow the teachings of the Lord of Light,
they may prove to be invaluable to the final

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:35.640
battle.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:41.099
Were she to help Jon Snow and Daenerys fight
the Night King's army in their hour of need,

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:45.420
she might even be invited to remain without
fear of persecution for her past actions,

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:48.120
and die on Westerosian soil as she intends
to.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:54.099
Get ready to spend more time at the ancestral
home of Balerion the Dread, because rumor

00:03:54.099 --> 00:03:58.480
has it that the major players will all be
meeting once again in the Dragonpit in Season

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:01.100
8 — and for much longer this time, too.

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:05.900
Watchers on the Wall reports that filming
at the Roman ruins of Itálica in Seville

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:09.740
were scheduled from April 23th to May 19th,
2018.

00:04:10.209 --> 00:04:14.200
That's nearly four weeks, which is quadruple
the time the crew spent filming there for

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:15.060
Season 7.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:20.320
Whether the scene is longer or just more action-packed,
it’s certain to be substantially bigger

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:21.700
and better than the last time.

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:27.200
What's more, there were no additional casting
calls for extras, which means it's probably

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:31.560
safe to assume that this particular scene
will once again feature only the main characters

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:32.500
we already know.

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:36.550
And if Sophie Turner's talk of filming in
Spain is a clue, then perhaps Sansa will get

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:38.320
to say her piece at the Dragonpit, too.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:43.680
Rumors from The Dubrovnik Times indicate that
the last scene of the entire series may very

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:45.600
well take place at King's Landing.

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:51.360
According to these reports, the scene would
have been shot in January 2018, with tents

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:55.690
in the old town of Dubrovnik being a big sign
that something was shot at King's Landing

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:57.100
with most of the main cast.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:02.620
No additional extras were called beyond the
main cast members, which is perhaps what caused

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:05.880
sources to speculate that it was, in fact,
the final scene.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:10.420
Nothing is official, of course, but surely
King's Landing — the infamous home of the

00:05:10.431 --> 00:05:15.120
Iron Throne — would be a fitting location
to end the series which is all about that

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:15.840
seat of power.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:20.970
Promisingly, the news that multiple main cast
members were present is also a good indication

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:24.220
that they probably don't all die in the second
War for the Dawn.

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:26.100
Thank the gods for that.

